// niri port: runtime "internal monitor off" switch -- written and removed by ~/bin/hyprctl
// when Omarchy's monitor scripts ask for hl.monitor({ disabled = true|false })
// (the clamshell reconcile, and the menu's Laptop Display toggle). Optional include, so
// "output enabled" is simply "the file is absent"; the file is the state.
//
// It MUST stay first, ahead of the output block below: niri keeps the *first* definition
// of a key, and a later duplicate block for an already-configured output is inert. Both
// halves of that were measured on niri 26.04 (2026-09-24) with a second block for eDP-1:
//   * trailing include -> `off` did nothing (`logical` unchanged);
//   * leading include  -> it applied (`logical` went null).
//
// One part of that reading was wrong, re-measured 2026-09-25: the *mode list* is built from
// the first block too, and this block carries no `modeline`, so while the overlay exists the
// panel sits on the 3840x2400 preferred mode rather than the tuned 2560x1600 one. The old
// note read `logical 2560x1600 at scale 1.5` as "the custom modeline below still applied",
// but 3840/1.5 x 2400/1.5 is exactly 2560x1600 -- that *was* the 4K fallback, as the journal
// settles it: `journalctl --user -b | grep "picking mode"` shows 18:27:46 picking
// "3840x2400" PREFERRED and 18:29:55 picking "2560x1600@59.97" USERDEF again, once the
// overlay was gone. The off-switch is still fine as it stands, because it is only ever in
// place while that output is off. Do NOT extend the trick to a key that is wanted *while the
// output is on*. Scale is the one that tempts, and it was tried: writing the Display panel's
// SCALE row through such an overlay dropped this panel to 4K for the rest of the session.
// The scale lives in the output block below instead, and the panel's SCALE row deliberately
// only runs `niri msg output … scale`, i.e. runtime-only -- it is this line that persists.
//
// monitor.kdl itself stays byte-identical to the repo mirror (scripts/kdl-sync.sh compares
// it); the overlay name is outside the seven *.kdl names that script walks.
include optional=true "output-toggle-off.kdl"

// Output / monitor configuration.
// You can configure outputs by their name, which you can find
// by running `niri msg outputs` while inside a niri instance.
// The built-in laptop monitor is usually called "eDP-1".
// Find more information on the wiki:
// https://niri-wm.github.io/niri/Configuration:-Outputs
output "eDP-1" {
    // Tuned for this machine: CSO1411 panel with custom EDID DTD2 = 2560x1600@60
    // (cvt -r timing, matches vantage "均衡（默认）" preset). Do NOT add a `mode`
    // line: naming the custom mode does not survive a reload (measured 2026-09-24)
    // and the panel falls back to 4K.
    // scale 1.6 = what the bar's Display panel last settled on; logical = 1600x1000.
    // This line is the only thing that outlives the session (see the top of this file).
    // 2.0 = an integer scale, crisper X11 apps, but 1280x800, i.e. a bigger UI than this.
    modeline 337.50 2880 2928 2960 3040 1800 1803 1809 1852 "+hsync" "-vsync"
    scale 1.8
    position x=0 y=0
}
